# This repository is consumed byte-wise. Waveguide Generator packages a checkout
# of a pinned commit into a deterministic archive, ships that archive inside its
# application layer, and its release workflow asserts that the Windows-built and
# macOS-built layers carry the same treeSha256. Without a rule here, that
# checkout inherits the build host's core.autocrlf -- true by default on Git for
# Windows -- and the two hosts build different archives from one commit.
#
# Measured 2026-09-07 on the then-pinned commit: 13 of 43 archive members
# differed, each longer by roughly a byte a line, and the archives hashed
# differently. The consumer pins its own checkout as well, because a pin can
# name a commit older than this line; this rule is what makes that belt and
# braces rather than a single point of failure.
#
# No blob in this repository contains CRLF today, so this changes no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# STEP fixtures are byte-exact CAD kernel output. Keep them out of line-ending
# normalisation and whitespace linting: the trailing spaces in an Open CASCADE
# AP214 file are the writer's own, and a fixture that is rewritten on checkout
# is no longer the file that was measured.
tests/fixtures/step/*.step -text -whitespace
